# Build trees. Two, because we routinely have a host-only and a CUDA build side
# by side (macOS + a remote GPU checkout).
build/
build-host/
build-*/
compile_commands.json

# Profiler output. These are large binaries (an ncu report is easily 100+ MB) and
# are regenerable. The *derived numbers* belong in RESULTS.md, which IS committed
# — commit the conclusion, not the raw capture.
# reports/: benchmark DATASETS are committed (one dir per run, Phase 5 stage 5f,
# DECISIONS.md Q10 -- RESULTS.md tables render from pinned datasets, so the
# datasets must be in the repo). Stray files written straight into reports/
# (e.g. alloc_bench run from the repo root) stay ignored. Profiler binaries
# (*.nsys-rep, *.ncu-rep, *.sqlite) stay ignored everywhere via the globals
# below, and are force-added deliberately when one is worth keeping.
reports/*
!reports/*/
logs/
*.nsys-rep
*.sqlite
*.ncu-rep
*.qdrep

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.cache/
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Python (tools/ plotting + reference generation only, never the runtime)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# Local copy of Northeastern RC's public docs (Explorer's user manual), kept as a
# reference -- it is what corrected this repo's "compute nodes have no network"
# claim in 2026-09. NOT committed: third-party, 97 MB (58 MB of it .mp4), and
# public upstream at https://github.com/northeastern-rc/rc-public-documentation.
# Ignored explicitly so a stray `git add -A` cannot put 97 MB into history.
HPC docs/
